# L4D2 Server CLI @TAG@

Linux x86_64 directory bundle; includes CPython @PYTHON_VERSION@. No system Python, venv or pip is required. The host needs glibc 2.31+; game management also needs running systemd and the game's 32-bit dependencies.

Download the matching archive and checksum from:
https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@/releases/tag/@TAG@

```bash
sha256sum -c l4d2-server-cli-@TAG@-linux-x86_64.sha256
tar -xzf l4d2-server-cli-@TAG@-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
cd l4d2-server-cli-@TAG@-linux-x86_64
sudo bash ./install.sh
l4d2 --version
l4d2 --help
l4d2 network check
sudo l4d2 server install --dir /opt/l4d2
sudo l4d2 server configure --name "My L4D2 Server" --visibility public
sudo l4d2 server start
```

The installer copies the complete verified CLI into /usr/local/lib/l4d2-server-cli/ and registers /usr/local/bin/l4d2. Both ordinary shells and sudo can use `l4d2` from any directory; the original extraction can then be removed. An unrelated existing command is never overwritten. Reinstalling the same bundle is supported; upgrades switch the command only after verification. Game files and services are not changed by this CLI installation.

For portable use, keep the entire extracted directory, including _internal/, and run `./l4d2`. Do not copy only the executable. Run `l4d2 auth login` as an ordinary user if account authentication is needed; do not use sudo for login.

The CLI does not open firewalls or cloud security groups. Allow the game UDP port and verify joining from an external client. SteamCMD, game files, account caches, server configuration and test reports are not included.

Installation and known limitations:
https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@/blob/@TAG@/README.md

Runtime provenance and library requirements are in build-info.json; FILES.sha256 verifies unpacked regular files. Third-party license texts are in licenses/. This is a preview; a CLI build check does not certify full game installation, all distributions or gameplay.
